<a id="finding-compliance-connection-analyzer-standard-resource-operations"></a>
### Connection Analyzer does not use the documented ARM resource operation templates

**Severity:** medium

**Gap:** The new resource-style CRUD and list operations use legacy action helpers and manual routes instead of standard ARM resource-operation templates.

<details>
<summary><strong>Expected</strong></summary>

CRUDL uses ArmResourceRead, ArmResourceCreateOrReplace, ArmTagsPatch or ArmCustomPatch, ArmResourceDelete, and ArmResourceListByParent; actions are reserved for behavior outside CRUDL.

**Guidance:** [ARM resource operations — Recommended operations and custom actions](https://azure.github.io/typespec-azure/docs/howtos/arm/resource-operations/)

**Documented ARM child-resource operations**

```tsp
get is ArmResourceRead<Resource>;
createOrUpdate is ArmResourceCreateOrReplaceAsync<Resource>;
update is ArmCustomPatchSync<Resource, PatchRequest>;
delete is ArmResourceDeleteSync<Resource>;
listByParent is ArmResourceListByParent<Resource>;
```

</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>Actual</strong></summary>

ConnectionAnalyzer PUT, GET, PATCH, and DELETE use Legacy.RoutedOperations action helpers, while list is manually routed.

